{"addedOn":10,"avgRating":["fa fa-star-o","fa fa-star-o","fa fa-star-o","fa fa-star-o","fa fa-star-o"],"breadcrumbsHtml":"<a href=\"https://docs-be.progress.com/bundle/openedge-abl-reference-117\">OpenEdge Development: ABL Reference</a>\n<span><i class=\"fa fa-angle-right\"></i>\n</span>\n<a href=\"https://docs-be.progress.com/bundle/openedge-abl-reference-117/page/ABL-Syntax-Reference.html\">ABL Syntax Reference</a>\n<span><i class=\"fa fa-angle-right\"></i>\n</span>\n<span class=\"active\">+ Unary positive operator</span>\n","class":"manual","created":2879,"dislikeurl":"https://docs-be.progress.com/dislike/310868","html":"<article class=\"hascomments\" data-page=\"bundle:openedge-abl-reference-117/enus/Unary-positive-operator.html\" id=\"bundle:openedge-abl-reference-117/enus/Unary-positive-operator.html\"><main role=\"main\"><article aria-labelledby=\"ariaid-title1\" class=\"dita\" id=\"Unary-positive-operator\" role=\"article\">\n  <h1 class=\"title topictitle1 reference\" id=\"ariaid-title1\">+ Unary positive operator</h1>\n  \n  <div class=\"body refbody\">\n    <section class=\"section\">\n      <p class=\"p\">Preserves the positive or negative value of\na numeric expression. Do not confuse this operator with the addition\noperator that you use to add expressions together.</p>\n    </section>\n    <section class=\"section\" id=\"Unary-positive-operator__syntax_GC151R2678969\"><h2 class=\"title sectiontitle\" id=\"d222749e101\">Syntax</h2>\n      \n      <table class=\"table frame-all\" id=\"Unary-positive-operator__idGDE1UQ2661658\"><caption></caption><colgroup><col style=\"width:100%\" /></colgroup><tbody class=\"tbody\">\n            <tr class=\"row rowsep-0\">\n              <td class=\"entry colsep-1 rowsep-1\">\n                <pre class=\"pre codeblock\"><code>+ <var class=\"keyword varname\">expression</var></code></pre>\n              </td>\n            </tr>\n          </tbody></table>\n      <dl class=\"dl parml\">\n        \n          <dt class=\"dt pt dlterm\">\n            <var class=\"keyword varname\">expression</var>\n          </dt>\n          <dd class=\"dd pd\">An expression whose value is numeric.</dd>\n        \n      </dl>\n    </section>\n    <section class=\"section\" id=\"Unary-positive-operator__example_GC151S2678975\"><h2 class=\"title sectiontitle\" id=\"d222749e144\">Example</h2>\n      \n      <p class=\"p\">In\nthe <span class=\"ph filepath\">r-unpos.p</span> example, the sign of <code class=\"ph codeph\">CreditLimit</code> is\npreserved as is the sign of the sum of <code class=\"ph codeph\">CreditLimit</code> +\n100. The unary positive is not necessary; it is used simply to document\nthe procedure, as shown:</p>\n      <p class=\"p\">\n        <strong class=\"ph b\">r-unpos.p</strong>\n      </p>\n      <table class=\"table frame-all\" id=\"Unary-positive-operator__idGDE1UR2661663\"><caption></caption><colgroup><col style=\"width:100%\" /></colgroup><tbody class=\"tbody\">\n            <tr class=\"row rowsep-0\">\n              <td class=\"entry colsep-1 rowsep-1\">\n                <pre class=\"pre codeblock\"><code>DEFINE VARIABLE old-max NO-UNDO LIKE CreditLimit LABEL &quot;Old Limit&quot;.\n\nFOR EACH Customer:\n  old-max =+ Customer.CreditLimit.\n  Customer.CreditLimit =+ (Customer.CreditLimit + 100).\n  DISPLAY Customer.Name old-max Customer.CreditLimit.\nEND.</code></pre>\n              </td>\n            </tr>\n          </tbody></table>\n    </section>\n    <section class=\"section\" id=\"Unary-positive-operator__see-also_GC151T2678983\"><h2 class=\"title sectiontitle\" id=\"d222749e188\">See also</h2>\n      \n      <p class=\"p\">\n        <a class=\"xref\" data-bundleid=\"openedge-abl-reference-117\" data-navpath=\"Unary-negative-operator.html\" href=\"https://docs-be.progress.com/bundle/openedge-abl-reference-117/page/Unary-negative-operator.html#Unary-negative-operator\">- Unary negative operator</a>\n      </p>\n    </section>\n  </div>\n<nav role=\"navigation\"><div class=\"familylinks\"><div class=\"previouslink\"><strong>Previous topic:</strong> <a class=\"link\" data-bundleid=\"openedge-abl-reference-117\" data-navpath=\"Single-line-comments.html\" href=\"https://docs-be.progress.com/bundle/openedge-abl-reference-117/page/Single-line-comments.html\">// Single-line comments</a></div><div class=\"nextlink\"><strong>Next topic:</strong> <a class=\"link\" data-bundleid=\"openedge-abl-reference-117\" data-navpath=\"Addition-operator.html\" href=\"https://docs-be.progress.com/bundle/openedge-abl-reference-117/page/Addition-operator.html\">+ Addition operator</a></div></div></nav><nav class=\"related-links\" role=\"navigation\"></nav></article></main></article>\n","isWatched":false,"labelText":"Product; Product > OpenEdge; Product > OpenEdge > Version 11.7; Format; Format > Documentation","likes":0,"likeurl":"https://docs-be.progress.com/like/310868","myDocsURL":null,"numOfPageViews":0,"numOfRatingsText":"<span>0 Ratings","revised":2879,"showWatch":false,"topicMeta":[["bookowner","oe11docs"],["bookrights","oe11docs"],["bundle","openedge-abl-reference-117"],["data","OEInformationHub/Product"],["data","OEInformationHub/Product/product_openedge"],["data","OEInformationHub/Product/product_openedge/product_openedge_117"],["data","OEInformationHub/format"],["data","OEInformationHub/format/format_documentation"],["organization","oe11docs"]],"topicTitle":"+ Unary positive operator","topicurl":"https://docs-be.progress.com/bundle/openedge-abl-reference-117/page/Unary-positive-operator.html","type":"Manual"}